# The `security` domain follows Symfony's convention of message-as-key: the login page renders
# `error.messageKey|trans(error.messageData, 'security')`, so a missing catalog entry falls back to
# the English message itself rather than an opaque key. Framework auth messages ("Invalid
# credentials." etc.) already ship translated in symfony/security-core; only app-specific auth
# messages shown on the login screen are listed here.

msgid "Your account is locked. If you believe this is a mistake, you can appeal."
msgstr "Your account is locked. If you believe this is a mistake, you can appeal."
